WEBVTT

00:00:04.090 --> 00:00:08.500
Mobile Suit Zeta Gundam

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:15.580
ima wa ugokenai sore ga sadame dakedo

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:15.580
Right now I can't move... That is my fate, but...

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:20.720
akirame wa shinai mou mezameta kara

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:20.720
I won't give up anymore because I have awakened.

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:25.890
moeru tokimeki wa jidai wo utsushi

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:25.890
My burning, throbbing heart reflects the era...

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:31.060
iro azayaka ni moesakaru honoo

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:31.060
It has the color of vividly blazing flames...

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:35.820
Crying ima wa mienaku tomo

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:35.820
Crying, though I can't see it right now...

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:40.350
Searching michi shirube wa ukabu

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:40.350
Searching, a guidepost floats up ahead.

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:43.170
I wanna have a pure time!

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:48.280
Everyone's a noble mind!

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:53.500
soko ni nokotta wakasa toridashi

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:53.500
I'll take out what remains of my youth there,

00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:55.980
Believing a sign of Zeta,

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:00.540
beyond the hard times from now!

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:06.320
kawaku kuchibiru nureteiru nara

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:06.320
If these dry lips become wet,

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:11.460
toki wo norikoe atsui jidai e to

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:11.460
Beyond time, towards a passionate era,

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:16.500
utsuru darou to shinjiteiru kara

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:16.500
Because I believe it will move...

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:19.060
Believing a sign of Zeta,

00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:23.690
beyond the hard times from now...

00:01:49.650 --> 00:01:53.520
Perhaps it might have been
a living being with a soul.

00:01:54.020 --> 00:01:58.680
However, now the soul
will likely never be at peace.

00:02:02.790 --> 00:02:07.820
Here exists a planet where intelligent
life forms that call themselves humans live.

00:02:07.900 --> 00:02:10.130
The humans here took the act
of giving birth...

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:15.200
...and raising children
far too much for granted.

00:02:15.910 --> 00:02:20.690
The Dark Side of the Moon

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:40.920
How does it look?

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:42.360
We're almost done.

00:02:42.430 --> 00:02:44.260
We've reduced play of the control stick.

00:02:44.740 --> 00:02:46.230
I'm impressed.

00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:48.030
Are you really going to pilot this?

00:02:48.110 --> 00:02:50.370
I'm not about to make someone
who's exhausted...

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:52.310
...from battle test this out.

00:02:52.380 --> 00:02:53.340
Please keep me out of it.

00:02:53.680 --> 00:02:56.200
The controller on the mobile suit deck
has already cleared this.

00:02:56.950 --> 00:02:59.850
- When are you going?
- In about fifteen minutes.

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:00.610
Okay, then.

00:03:15.330 --> 00:03:16.730
Leave me alone!

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:18.770
Stop sulking, Kamille.

00:03:22.610 --> 00:03:23.540
Lieutenant Quattro!

00:03:23.610 --> 00:03:27.700
Sorry. But you can feel free to tell us if
you have something in your mind.

00:03:29.250 --> 00:03:31.610
There's no way I can.

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:33.120
Why not get some exercise?

00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:35.120
Don't say it so casually.

00:03:35.190 --> 00:03:37.250
Did something happen between you
and Lieutenant Lila?

00:03:38.060 --> 00:03:39.890
Please leave, Lieutenant.

00:03:39.960 --> 00:03:42.650
Lieutenant Emma,
you're on probation, right?

00:03:43.390 --> 00:03:46.730
This room doesn't have
a surveillance camera...

00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:48.100
...so you can't come in, Lieutenant.

00:03:48.530 --> 00:03:51.630
I'm sorry to disappoint you, but from today on,
I'm free to do as I wish.

00:03:51.970 --> 00:03:53.940
I've been accepted
as a crewmember of the A.E.U.G..

00:03:56.310 --> 00:03:58.780
That's one thing I wanted to tell you about.

00:04:03.010 --> 00:04:04.000
May I be seated?

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:05.840
You invited yourself in.

00:04:05.920 --> 00:04:09.680
The Lieutenant's concerned
that you might be angry...

00:04:09.750 --> 00:04:13.320
...with the Argama crew
for trying to make you a soldier.

00:04:14.890 --> 00:04:16.920
Lieutenant.

00:04:16.990 --> 00:04:19.160
Why don't you speak with your own words?

00:04:19.530 --> 00:04:20.500
Huh?

00:04:21.530 --> 00:04:24.590
I apologize. I thought...

00:04:24.670 --> 00:04:28.230
...that perhaps you felt something during
your battle against Lieutenant Lila...

00:04:28.310 --> 00:04:30.470
...and that you don't know how to deal with it.

00:04:31.740 --> 00:04:34.230
You've got a great imagination.

00:04:34.310 --> 00:04:35.870
Are you suggesting that I can read
an enemy's moods and feelings...

00:04:35.950 --> 00:04:41.390
...through the armor of a mobile suit,
like a Newtype?

00:04:45.760 --> 00:04:48.190
Lieutenant Lila
was a very strong opponent...

00:04:48.260 --> 00:04:50.780
...so I fought desperately and I won, that's all.

00:04:50.860 --> 00:04:52.350
I regret nothing.

00:04:53.300 --> 00:04:56.030
You're lying, Kamille Bidan!

00:04:59.040 --> 00:05:02.970
- Where are you going?!
- You heard Lieutenant Quattro.

00:05:03.040 --> 00:05:05.010
I'm going for some exercise.

00:05:10.110 --> 00:05:13.080
At the Argama, they're saying...

00:05:13.150 --> 00:05:15.380
...the whereabouts of Amuro Ray
is unknown, right?

00:05:21.560 --> 00:05:22.620
I...

00:05:22.690 --> 00:05:26.220
I met Amuro Ray once
about two and a half years ago.

00:05:26.760 --> 00:05:31.720
I met him over at Cheyenne during a trip
with my girlfriend in a gas-powered car.

00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:36.400
In front of a big mansion.

00:05:36.970 --> 00:05:41.140
At the time we were joking
that such a gloomy young man...

00:05:41.210 --> 00:05:43.910
...living on his parents' inheritance
still exists to this day.

00:05:45.050 --> 00:05:48.540
I thought the young man was deeply tired...

00:05:48.620 --> 00:05:50.680
...yet kept dreaming about his future.

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:54.320
And that was the impression
I got from him, but...

00:05:54.390 --> 00:05:58.390
I realized recently that the young man
was in fact Amuro Ray.

00:05:59.660 --> 00:06:01.150
Did he say who he was?

00:06:02.030 --> 00:06:03.520
No, he didn't.

00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:05.570
I realized it after coming out to outer space.

00:06:15.380 --> 00:06:19.440
After meeting someone like Lt. Quattro
I became certain the young man was Amuro.

00:06:20.080 --> 00:06:23.950
I realized he was Amuro Ray, tormented
for not being able to return to outer space.

00:06:24.620 --> 00:06:27.320
- You're just imagining things.
- No, I'm not.

00:06:28.390 --> 00:06:31.620
<i>I came to the Argama because of...</i>

00:06:31.700 --> 00:06:35.100
<i>...that mysterious young man.</i>

00:06:35.170 --> 00:06:36.900
<i>And I realized that because of the air</i>
<i>in the Argama.</i>

00:06:36.970 --> 00:06:43.970
<i>And as I began to see that this air is what</i>
<i>that young man desired, what he wanted...</i>

00:06:44.940 --> 00:06:48.240
<i>...I clearly realized that the young man</i>
<i>was Amuro.</i>

00:06:48.950 --> 00:06:53.850
Then do you believe there's someone
like Char Aznable on this ship?

00:06:53.920 --> 00:06:55.390
Perhaps I do.

00:06:56.290 --> 00:07:01.090
I'm no longer driven by impulse like I was
when wanting to board the Argama.

00:07:01.160 --> 00:07:03.350
I'm much more relaxed now.

00:07:03.430 --> 00:07:05.160
Then you've met Char.

00:07:08.030 --> 00:07:09.470
Huh? What did you just say?

00:07:09.530 --> 00:07:11.430
I just said, "You want to meet Char,
don't you?"

00:07:11.500 --> 00:07:13.830
No, you said that I had already met Char.

00:07:13.900 --> 00:07:15.670
I didn't say that!

00:07:16.210 --> 00:07:18.110
<i>All crew, take level two battle stations!</i>

00:07:18.540 --> 00:07:21.510
- Pursuers?
- I never said such a thing!

00:07:21.880 --> 00:07:23.680
Yes, you did! You said I met Char!

00:07:32.290 --> 00:07:34.280
<i>We're only testing the balance of it</i>
<i>when fully equipped!</i>

00:07:34.360 --> 00:07:36.330
<i>Return as soon as you're done!</i>

00:07:36.530 --> 00:07:37.220
Roger!

00:07:37.290 --> 00:07:40.230
<i>Enemy vessel located!</i>
<i>Deploy a scout mobile suit!</i>

00:07:40.930 --> 00:07:42.900
<i>Did you hear that, Jerid?!</i>
<i>Go track them down!</i>

00:07:43.300 --> 00:07:44.270
Roger!

00:07:51.910 --> 00:07:54.640
All you need to do is confirm
where the Argama's hiding.

00:07:54.710 --> 00:07:56.410
- Can you hear me?!
- <i>I heard you!</i>

00:07:59.850 --> 00:08:01.510
A Galbaldy just launched?

00:08:05.360 --> 00:08:09.380
Lila, will you guide me?

00:08:13.360 --> 00:08:15.330
We'll make it appear like we're headed
for Granada...

00:08:15.400 --> 00:08:17.370
...and then quickly change our
course to Amman!

00:08:18.840 --> 00:08:21.400
- <i>Keep it still!</i>
- <i>Is it only the Mk. II?!</i>

00:08:22.210 --> 00:08:24.170
<i>Lieutenant Quattro will follow!</i>

00:08:24.980 --> 00:08:25.770
Thank you!

00:08:29.050 --> 00:08:32.020
Aren't you going to launch
unless I lure you out, Gundam Mk. II?

00:08:34.720 --> 00:08:35.580
Good!

00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:48.520
Is he insane?!

00:08:48.600 --> 00:08:51.400
- Kamille, launching!
- <i>Enemy's coming from the front!</i>

00:08:59.810 --> 00:09:01.940
What's the idea of firing
as I'm taking off?!

00:09:05.150 --> 00:09:06.450
<i>Enemy at ten o'clock!</i>

00:09:06.520 --> 00:09:09.040
I'm launching!
Cover me with the beam cannons!

00:09:22.130 --> 00:09:24.070
Did the bastard come out?!

00:09:32.910 --> 00:09:35.640
A mobile suit belonging to Lila's unit!
Is this person her subordinate?

00:09:55.870 --> 00:09:58.100
<i>Are you the bastard who shot Lila down?!</i>

00:09:58.970 --> 00:10:01.130
<i>I will destroy you in single combat!</i>

00:10:01.210 --> 00:10:02.370
With a mobile suit?!

00:10:02.740 --> 00:10:06.510
You probably don't know Lila,
but to me, she was my teacher!

00:10:06.880 --> 00:10:09.510
You think you're the only one
who's lost someone?!

00:10:09.580 --> 00:10:12.950
Will she be happy?!
Will she come back to life?!

00:10:13.480 --> 00:10:14.780
Stop talking as if you know everything!

00:10:26.030 --> 00:10:26.890
Kamille!

00:10:34.510 --> 00:10:36.530
Kamille is being drawn away
from the Argama.

00:10:36.610 --> 00:10:38.580
He appears to be chased by a Galbaldy!

00:10:38.640 --> 00:10:40.010
Lieutenant Quattro, where are you?!

00:10:40.080 --> 00:10:43.740
Turn downward! Take the direct route
to Granada! Altitude five hundred!

00:10:48.320 --> 00:10:50.480
Incredible... his instincts are inhuman!

00:10:56.030 --> 00:10:56.990
What?!

00:10:59.000 --> 00:11:01.230
It jumps this much even without the use
of the vernier!

00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:07.700
Once again, you're unnecessarily
making me take away lives!

00:11:10.640 --> 00:11:11.700
What?!

00:11:11.780 --> 00:11:14.070
You're not the only one
special around here!

00:11:14.380 --> 00:11:15.870
I am a member of the Titans after all!

00:11:33.860 --> 00:11:38.270
Even if you are a Newtype, I bet
this is your first battle on the Moon!

00:11:45.180 --> 00:11:47.140
Like this?!

00:11:51.350 --> 00:11:53.320
It's out of power?!

00:12:12.600 --> 00:12:15.270
The Argama's not where
we saw the line of fire?!

00:12:15.340 --> 00:12:18.310
- What about the scout Galbaldy?!
- No response, sir!

00:12:19.010 --> 00:12:21.380
Blex must have eliminated him.

00:12:27.820 --> 00:12:28.980
Darn it!

00:12:33.860 --> 00:12:37.090
Those powers aren't what one would expect
from a child!

00:12:37.160 --> 00:12:39.560
What is this child?! Lila!

00:12:46.140 --> 00:12:48.200
Newtypes aren't supermen, you know!

00:12:54.240 --> 00:12:55.770
What?!

00:12:56.980 --> 00:12:58.240
Did I get him?!

00:13:07.420 --> 00:13:08.650
Gotcha!

00:13:18.600 --> 00:13:20.570
Lila, watch me finish him!

00:13:25.780 --> 00:13:26.940
Reinforcements?!

00:13:27.010 --> 00:13:28.440
Where's Kacricon?!

00:13:37.090 --> 00:13:40.060
Aren't I even capable of avenging
a fallen comrade...

00:13:41.760 --> 00:13:43.730
<i>Can you make it alone, Kamille?</i>

00:13:44.090 --> 00:13:46.620
<i>I'm all right. I can still move!</i>

00:13:47.770 --> 00:13:50.430
I'm terribly sorry. My rifle got destroyed.

00:13:50.800 --> 00:13:52.770
You played right into the enemy's hands,
didn't you?

00:13:53.240 --> 00:13:54.830
We're returning to the Argama!

00:13:55.170 --> 00:13:59.170
He's really torn it apart this time!
We'll have to completely replace the leg!

00:13:59.240 --> 00:14:00.640
- The rest we'll do later!
- That enemy...

00:14:00.710 --> 00:14:02.910
...wasn't part of the Galbaldy team, was he?

00:14:02.980 --> 00:14:05.180
No, he was Lieutenant Jerid Messa.

00:14:06.680 --> 00:14:09.620
It's as if he was possessed by
Lieutenant Lila's grudge.

00:14:09.690 --> 00:14:12.280
Did you feel that too, Lieutenant Quattro?

00:14:12.990 --> 00:14:15.250
You're very perceptive to realize that.

00:14:15.330 --> 00:14:16.850
Thank you, sir.

00:14:16.930 --> 00:14:19.590
However, I'd have to say
your inexperience shows...

00:14:19.660 --> 00:14:22.060
...in the way you were lured away by
a single mobile suit.

00:14:23.630 --> 00:14:27.660
Watch out, or you'll be killed next time.

00:14:31.040 --> 00:14:33.340
I'm not going to die!

00:14:44.490 --> 00:14:46.750
<i>It's a pleasure to see you back safely</i>
<i>from your long journey. At Granada...</i>

00:14:46.820 --> 00:14:49.260
I'm in no mood for flattery!

00:14:49.560 --> 00:14:52.120
<i>...we're issuing 20% discount coupons</i>
<i>to crew members.</i>

00:15:44.080 --> 00:15:45.510
Come in.

00:15:48.220 --> 00:15:49.880
Welcome back, Captain.

00:15:50.290 --> 00:15:53.450
Kignan, I am Lieutenant Quattro.

00:15:53.520 --> 00:15:55.960
To me you are Captain Char Aznable.

00:15:56.860 --> 00:15:58.380
How are things at Granada?

00:15:58.460 --> 00:16:01.490
The Alexandria and two other vessels
have entered the space port.

00:16:01.570 --> 00:16:03.730
Will it work?

00:16:03.800 --> 00:16:06.000
Well, Anaheim's also counting on it.

00:16:06.070 --> 00:16:07.760
Did something happen?

00:16:07.840 --> 00:16:10.400
- This is a photo of the asteroid belt.
- What?

00:16:11.210 --> 00:16:13.870
We could determine from spectral analysis
that this is a nuclear pulse.

00:16:13.940 --> 00:16:15.670
Nuclear pulse?

00:16:16.680 --> 00:16:18.810
- It must be the Axis?
- Yes, sir.

00:16:18.880 --> 00:16:22.220
They began their journey to Earth
some time ago.

00:16:22.720 --> 00:16:23.980
To Earth?

00:16:24.520 --> 00:16:25.420
Yes, sir.

00:16:26.520 --> 00:16:28.490
So Zeon's ghost has begun its move.

00:16:30.060 --> 00:16:32.590
Has Haman Karn turned twenty years old?

00:16:33.330 --> 00:16:34.300
Yes.

00:16:34.770 --> 00:16:37.030
There's one other thing
that's been bothering me, sir.

00:16:38.670 --> 00:16:40.140
Gryps has started moving.

00:16:41.140 --> 00:16:42.870
Green Noa has?

00:16:42.940 --> 00:16:44.410
Damn Bask!!

00:16:49.350 --> 00:16:50.640
<i>Lieutenant Quattro?</i>

00:16:50.710 --> 00:16:53.210
<i>I have a message here</i>
<i>from Mr. Wong Lee.</i>

00:16:54.020 --> 00:16:58.080
<i>"Please meet me tomorrow at 10 AM at</i>
<i>'Macdaniel' on Eastern Avenue. "</i>

00:16:58.290 --> 00:16:59.690
Macdaniel?

00:16:59.760 --> 00:17:01.520
It's a hamburger restaurant, sir.

00:17:01.590 --> 00:17:03.290
Very well. Thank you.

00:17:04.090 --> 00:17:07.120
<i>That will be fifteen cents, please.</i>

00:17:07.200 --> 00:17:10.500
<i>Thank you very much.</i>
<i>Please feel free to use our services again.</i>

00:17:11.770 --> 00:17:14.000
Is this all they can supply?!

00:17:14.500 --> 00:17:16.800
What's going on at Granada?!

00:17:17.770 --> 00:17:21.300
Granada's also waiting for supplies
from Earth, they say.

00:17:21.380 --> 00:17:23.510
That's just an excuse not to help us.

00:17:23.780 --> 00:17:26.410
- Those damn A.E.U.G. supporters!
- Sir...?

00:17:26.480 --> 00:17:27.350
What is it?!

00:17:27.420 --> 00:17:29.440
Lieutenant Jerid has returned.

00:17:29.520 --> 00:17:33.110
Didn't he hear that he was suspended?!

00:17:33.190 --> 00:17:35.160
Throw him into the brig.

00:17:35.330 --> 00:17:36.620
Yes, sir!

00:17:42.130 --> 00:17:45.190
Lock me up, or do whatever you wish!

00:17:46.100 --> 00:17:49.870
If it's the RB unit, there's no need
to play with the circuit. Hand it all over to me.

00:17:51.040 --> 00:17:54.410
I see you're qualified not only in fighting
battles, but as a quartermaster as well.

00:17:55.210 --> 00:17:59.670
I'll see what I can do about getting
some wine, Mr. Military-Law-Offender.

00:17:59.750 --> 00:18:01.180
Maybe later.

00:18:01.250 --> 00:18:02.080
Lieutenant Jerid.

00:18:03.020 --> 00:18:07.250
Do I need your permission
to avenge the death of Lieutenant Lila?

00:18:08.260 --> 00:18:12.060
I got my hands on a little information...
and am on my way out.

00:18:12.130 --> 00:18:13.220
Where to?

00:18:13.300 --> 00:18:16.560
I have direct approval for this project
from Lieutenant Commander Jamaican.

00:18:17.570 --> 00:18:22.270
If I find myself in need of reinforcements,
I'll alert them that you're available...

00:18:22.340 --> 00:18:23.970
...but I can't take you with me now.

00:18:24.840 --> 00:18:26.900
Do as you wish.

00:18:26.980 --> 00:18:28.410
You don't need anyone's permission.

00:18:28.880 --> 00:18:30.940
Then get some rest for the time being.

00:18:34.720 --> 00:18:37.150
- Did you get any sleep last night?
- Yes!

00:18:37.220 --> 00:18:39.480
True gravity feels so comfortable.

00:18:39.890 --> 00:18:41.320
But what a surprise.

00:18:41.390 --> 00:18:44.590
I never expected to find a city close
to Granada that supports the A.E.U.G..

00:18:44.660 --> 00:18:45.920
I agree.

00:18:46.000 --> 00:18:49.400
There's even a newly built battleship
at the spaceport's farthest dock.

00:18:52.740 --> 00:18:54.500
What is that mountain?

00:18:54.570 --> 00:18:57.370
I heard it's made from the ruins of a colony.

00:18:57.810 --> 00:18:58.900
A colony?

00:18:58.980 --> 00:19:01.170
I assume from the days
of the One Year War.

00:19:02.010 --> 00:19:03.980
A colony, destroyed in the war...!

00:19:19.030 --> 00:19:19.760
Here?

00:19:20.100 --> 00:19:24.230
I can now understand why
the Titans organization was formed.

00:19:24.570 --> 00:19:25.970
Can you really?

00:19:26.040 --> 00:19:29.800
Yes. After seeing Colony 30, yes I can.

00:19:30.810 --> 00:19:33.830
But the objective of the Titans is to get rid
of all remnants of the Zeon forces, right?

00:19:34.210 --> 00:19:37.540
<i>No, they're just using Zeon to their benefit.</i>

00:19:37.610 --> 00:19:38.580
<i>What?!</i>

00:19:39.320 --> 00:19:41.340
<i>I realized after entering Green Noa.</i>

00:19:41.420 --> 00:19:44.390
- <i>I...!</i>
- <i>You were being deceived by Bask...?</i>

00:19:44.620 --> 00:19:46.780
This is it. I'll take a look.

00:19:51.460 --> 00:19:53.590
The Commodore has arrived at Granada.

00:19:59.600 --> 00:20:00.830
Wong Lee!

00:20:00.900 --> 00:20:03.840
With the cooperation of all of you,
we were able to complete our initial plan.

00:20:04.980 --> 00:20:06.530
Lieutenant Quattro, thank you!

00:20:06.610 --> 00:20:12.210
I called you out today because I heard that
you're against the plan to attack Jaburo.

00:20:12.280 --> 00:20:13.750
I wanted to hear your opinion on this.

00:20:14.850 --> 00:20:16.980
One reason is our lack of battle power...

00:20:17.050 --> 00:20:19.820
...and another is any act of destruction
on Earth will pollute it.

00:20:19.890 --> 00:20:22.830
Besides, once we're in the
gravity well...

00:20:22.890 --> 00:20:25.420
...how do we escape it?

00:20:25.500 --> 00:20:27.360
When considering the overall strategy...

00:20:27.430 --> 00:20:29.400
...destroying Gryps
would seem to be a better plan.

00:20:29.870 --> 00:20:33.030
But Gryps is nothing but a tool
of the Earth Federation.

00:20:33.100 --> 00:20:37.130
Unless we attack its headquarters,
they'll just build another Gryps.

00:20:37.840 --> 00:20:40.670
However, Jaburo is the Earth Federation's
stronghold.

00:20:41.440 --> 00:20:45.400
If we crush it, Gryps will have
nowhere to turn to for supplies!

00:20:46.320 --> 00:20:48.250
In addition, the world would have to
recognize the A.E.U.G....

00:20:48.320 --> 00:20:50.750
...and public opinion will be on our side.

00:20:51.420 --> 00:20:54.150
Mr. Wong, I always understood you
to be an investor.

00:20:54.220 --> 00:20:55.780
Are you now considering
a career in politics?

00:20:56.590 --> 00:20:57.860
Don't be ridiculous!

00:20:58.860 --> 00:21:02.630
Have you made contact with Karaba,
our support forces on the Earth?

00:21:04.130 --> 00:21:06.300
Yes, I have! You can hand over
your mobile suits to Karaba...

00:21:06.370 --> 00:21:08.930
...and your pilots can return to space.

00:21:09.540 --> 00:21:11.770
You're asking the impossible.

00:21:21.150 --> 00:21:22.550
Miss Emma!

00:21:32.760 --> 00:21:35.290
<i>Lieutenant Emma!</i>
<i>Why are you assisting the A.E.U.G.?!</i>

00:21:35.370 --> 00:21:36.330
<i>Kacricon?!</i>

00:21:37.170 --> 00:21:38.900
<i>You wouldn't understand even if I told you.</i>

00:22:12.400 --> 00:22:13.330
Miss Emma! Hurry!

00:22:25.720 --> 00:22:27.440
He's not coming after us!

00:22:29.290 --> 00:22:30.580
Kacricon...!

00:22:47.270 --> 00:22:49.600
Oh, I can't help believing you

00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:56.020
kanarazu aeru to ano hi kara shinjiteita

00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:56.020
I've believed we're sure to meet again ever since that day

00:22:56.070 --> 00:23:01.400
kitto yobiau kokoro ga areba

00:22:56.070 --> 00:23:01.400
If we have heart, we'll be called together again

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:11.790
mugen no Energy yobisamasu

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:11.790
Awaken the infinite energy

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:17.420
aa kizutsukeau mae ni

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:17.420
Before you get hurt

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:23.510
dekiru koto sagashite Please

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:23.510
Find what you can do...Please

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:28.680
nagedasanai de kurushii toki koso

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:28.680
Don't throw it away because of this painful age

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:32.020
itsuka mita aoi sora wo

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:32.020
Until the day we gaze up again

00:23:32.030 --> 00:23:39.030
kitto anata to miageru hi made

00:23:32.030 --> 00:23:39.030
at the blue sky we once saw

00:23:45.440 --> 00:23:50.210
Char embarks on a mission
to capture a Titans battleship.

00:23:50.280 --> 00:23:53.340
It is an operation that Kamille is against.

00:23:54.050 --> 00:23:59.380
However, sensing Emma Sheen in danger,
Kamille rescues her in Amman.

00:23:59.750 --> 00:24:02.950
It is the revelation of another gift
Kamille possesses.

00:24:03.020 --> 00:24:07.560
Next on Mobile Suit Zeta Gundam,
"A New Bond".

00:24:07.470 --> 00:24:12.470
Next Episode

00:24:07.470 --> 00:24:12.470
A New Bond

00:24:08.630 --> 00:24:11.500
You will see the tears of time.
